course: dictionary
lesson: 13387
title: The hearth
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hearth is where a fire burns. It is the floor of a fireplace and the ground just in front of it. «The cat curled up on the hearth to keep warm.» The cat is near the fire, so the hearth is the warm place beside the flames.
explain: Look at the words around a new word to find its meaning. «Keep toys and paper away from the hearth.» Toys and paper could catch fire, so the hearth is a place with fire in it. Try swapping in «the floor by the fireplace» and check if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Hearth can also mean home and family, especially in a cosy, old-fashioned way. «They sat together by the hearth, warm and safe.» Here the word is about a feeling of home, not only a place. The phrase «hearth and home» means the home and family together.
fact: A hearth is the floor of a fireplace and the area in front of it, where the fire burns.
fact: «Hearth» is a noun, and its plural is «hearths».
fact: In the past, the hearth was the centre of the home: people cooked, kept warm and gathered there.
fact: «Hearth» can mean home and family life, as in «hearth and home».
fact: Keep toys, paper and clothes away from the hearth to stay safe.
exercise: «The dog slept on the hearth.» Where did the dog sleep? | In the garden | *On the floor by the fireplace | In the bath | On the roof
exercise: In «hearth and home», what does hearth mean? | A tall tree | A kind of bread | A loud noise | *Home and family
exercise: «Keep your paper and clothes away from the hearth.» Why? | The hearth needs them to cook | *The fire could catch them | They will get wet | They might be lost
test: In history lessons, why was the hearth the centre of the home? | Children played football there | People swam there | *People cooked, kept warm and gathered there | It was where the rain came in
test: Which sentence shows hearth meaning a cosy, safe, homely scene? | «The hearth was loud with cars and buses.» | «The rain fell on the hearth all day.» | *«The family sat by the hearth, sharing stories and tea.» | «The hearth was made of stone and hard to climb.»
exam: The noun hearth can have a plural. Which word is the plural of hearth? | hearthes | *hearths | hearthing | hearthed
